The room dataset scenarios of the ROS reference harness read sequences of the TUM RGB-D
benchmark, which ros_reference/datasets.txt lists by address and SHA-256:
rgbd_dataset_freiburg2_pioneer_360, rgbd_dataset_freiburg2_pioneer_slam,
rgbd_dataset_freiburg2_pioneer_slam2 and rgbd_dataset_freiburg2_pioneer_slam3. The
repository holds none of their data. run.sh --datasets fetches them from
https://cvg.cit.tum.de/data/datasets/rgbd-dataset into the dataset cache of the host.

The TUM RGB-D dataset is the work of the Computer Vision Group of the Technical University
of Munich and is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. Its authors ask that work which
uses it cite:

  J. Sturm, N. Engelhard, F. Endres, W. Burgard and D. Cremers. A Benchmark for the
  Evaluation of RGB-D SLAM Systems. Proceedings of the International Conference on
  Intelligent Robot Systems (IROS), October 2012.

The harness reads the depth frames and the ground truth of each sequence, keeps one depth
frame each scan period, and projects each kept frame to a 2-D scan; the committed
reference outputs hold statistics of the runs on those scans, never the data.

